---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CompReveal from '../../components/CompReveal.astro';
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const jobPosting = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'JobPosting',
  title: 'Senior Full-stack Developer (AI-empowered)',
  description: 'Senior full-stack developer who works alongside Claude as a primary tool, owning ambiguous problems end-to-end.',
  datePosted: new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10),
  employmentType: ['FULL_TIME'],
  hiringOrganization: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'TailorMind', sameAs: 'https://tailormind.io' },
  jobLocationType: 'TELECOMMUTE',
  applicantLocationRequirements: { '@type': 'Country', name: 'Peru' },
  qualifications: '5+ years full-stack engineering. Strong written reasoning. Demonstrated AI-tooling fluency.',
  responsibilities: 'Ship full-stack features end-to-end with Claude. Maintain a decision journal. Run premortems before major work.',
};
---
<Base lang="en" title="Senior Full-stack Developer (AI-empowered) — TailorMind">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jobPosting)} />

  <h1>Senior Full-stack Developer (AI-empowered)</h1>
  <p class="lead">Remote · <strong>Peru only this round</strong> · Senior · We pay for the tool you use</p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>TailorMind builds AI-empowered products. We are a small team that ships, measures, and iterates with discipline. Have a look at <a href="https://tailormind.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">tailormind.io</a> to see what we're working on.</p>

  <h2>The role</h2>
  <p>You will own ambiguous full-stack problems end-to-end, using Claude as your primary force multiplier. We do not measure typing speed — we measure <strong>criterio</strong>: the judgment to decide what to build, what to skip, when to ask, and when to commit.</p>

  <h3>You will</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Discover & scope.</strong> Turn vague product asks into a short written spec — problem.</li>
    <li><strong>Design.</strong> Pick the data model, API shape, and architecture.</li>
    <li><strong>Build.</strong> Implement end-to-end: schema/migrations, backend, API, frontend, infra. Claude (Code, API, agents) is your daily tool.</li>
    <li><strong>Test.</strong> Test and catch the bugs before they get into production. Unit where logic is tricky, integration where systems meet, e2e on the golden path.</li>
    <li><strong>Review & ship.</strong> Open small, well-described PRs.</li>
    <li><strong>Operate.</strong> Watch what you shipped: logs, metrics, errors. </li>
    <li><strong>Reflect.</strong> Keep a decision journal (what / why / expected / confidence %).</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>We expect</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>3+ years</strong> full-stack engineering, mid-to-senior trajectory.</li>
    <li>Strong TypeScript or Python (both is ideal). Comfortable across DB, API, UI, deploy.</li>
    <li>Strong written reasoning — short, clear, calibrated.</li>
    <li>Fluency with at least one frontier-model coding assistant (Claude Code / Cursor / Copilot).</li>
    <li>English: working level (read/write).</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Nice to have</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Prior remote experience in distributed teams.</li>
    <li>OSS contributions, technical writing, or talks.</li>
    <li>Experience building Claude Agent SDK / tool-use systems.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we offer</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Remote, async-first work.</li>
    <li><strong>Whichever agent tooling you prefer, paid for</strong> — Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, or whatever comes next. We use Claude Code daily and it is what we can support best, but if you work better with something else, we pay for that instead. What is not negotiable is that you use one.</li>
    <li>Contract under Peruvian law — <em>planilla</em> or <em>recibo por honorarios (RxH)</em>, to be defined.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What you're signing up for</h2>
  <p>Before we talk money, the part that usually goes unsaid.</p>
  <p><strong>We are two people.</strong> There's no QA team, no DevOps, nobody handing you finished specs. What you decide to build is what exists. That's real freedom and it's also real weight: there's nowhere to hide when something breaks.</p>
  <p><strong>We're a startup, and startups die.</strong> We don't have a round that guarantees three years of runway. That's a real risk, not a figure of speech. If you have a stable job today, a mortgage, or people who depend on predictable income, this may not be for you — and saying so costs you nothing in this process.</p>
  <p><strong>We don't want to talk you into it.</strong> If you need convincing, that's already the answer. We'd rather you ask the uncomfortable questions: how much runway, where the revenue comes from today, what happens if it doesn't work. We'll answer with numbers in the interview, not with enthusiasm.</p>
  <p><strong>What is on offer:</strong> decisions get made with you in the room, not three levels up; real AI tooling with budget to use it; and a range of impact that would take years at a large company. If this works, you'll have built the product — not a module of the product.</p>

  <h2>How the work actually goes, and why the process changed</h2>
  <p>This is not "we use AI to go faster". It is a different way of working, and you should see it before you apply.</p>
  <p><strong>Agents write the code.</strong> You run several fronts at once, each with its own agent and branch, and you spend the day deciding: what gets in, which plan is wrong, which output ships, what gets cut. In a normal week you will not type a whole function.</p>
  <p><strong>What is scarce is no longer writing — it is your attention.</strong> With three agents in parallel, more finished work arrives than one person can read. That is where the decision that matters shows up: what you read in full, what you sample, what you approve unread. And it is paid for: whatever you do not review, production reviews for you.</p>
  <p><strong>You answer for what you merge, whether you wrote it or not.</strong> "The model gave me that" is not an explanation for why something is in production. You can say you did not verify it — that costs you nothing — but saying it after shipping does.</p>
  <p><strong>That is why the hiring process changed.</strong> A "build me a CRUD this afternoon" take-home measured something we no longer do: a model writes that in ten minutes. The new one lasts 30 minutes, the requirements arrive while you work, and <strong>they do not all fit</strong> — because that is what a real week looks like, and because the only thing that separates people in that scenario is judgement: what you pick, what you sacrifice, and what you put in writing.</p>
  <p>If what you love is three uninterrupted hours of writing code, this role will frustrate you. If what you love is your judgement multiplied by five, it is exactly this one.</p>

  <h2>Compensation</h2>
  <p>Base monthly compensation expressed as a multiple of the Peruvian minimum wage (RMV), in PEN.</p>
  <CompReveal lang="en" />
  <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500">Revealing logs your email to our pipeline. We use it only for this hiring process. See <a href={`${b}/en/privacy/`}>privacy</a>.</p>

  <p><a href={`${b}/en/apply/`} class="not-prose inline-block px-4 py-2 rounded bg-[color:var(--color-brand-600)] text-white">Apply now</a></p>
</Base>
